// expect-error: cannot assign to expression — not an lvalue
// BUG-1525: `@truncate(u32, x) = 3;` compiled and the write was thrown away
// (x stayed 1); `~x = 5` / `(u32)x = 3` reached GCC. The lvalue rule is now an
// allow-list of places.
u32 main() {
    u32 x = 1;
    @truncate(u32, x) = 3;
    return x;
}
